# herdr-orchestrator configuration (template)
#
# Copy to ~/.config/herdr-orchestrator/config and uncomment what you need.
# scripts/herd.sh sources this file as shell code on every call, so use plain
# shell syntax (no spaces around "="). Set HERD_CONFIG in the environment to
# use a different path.
#
# This file controls mechanics only. Which model implements or reviews what
# belongs in ~/.config/herdr-orchestrator/policy.md (see policy.example.md).

# --- Backends ---------------------------------------------------------------

# Allowlist of backends herd.sh may start, comma-separated. Empty or unset:
# every installed backend is allowed. Use it to keep work and private
# accounts apart, e.g. only approved backends on a work machine.
# BACKENDS=claude,codex,pi

# --- Default models (used when start/exec gets no --model) ------------------
# Unset: the backend's own default applies. Slugs depend on your accounts.

# MODEL_CLAUDE=opus
# MODEL_CODEX="<model>"
# MODEL_AGY="<model>"
# MODEL_OPENCODE="<provider/model>"
# MODEL_COPILOT="<model>"
# MODEL_GROK="<model>"
# MODEL_KIMI="<model>"
# MODEL_MUSE="<model>"
# pi has no fallback: without --model or MODEL_PI, start/exec refuse.
# MODEL_PI="<provider/model>"

# Provider prefix for opencode models given without "provider/". No default.
# OPENCODE_PROVIDER="<provider>"

# Provider for pi when --model is not "provider/id". No default; without it
# such a pi start fails.
# HERD_PI_PROVIDER="<provider>"

# Answer pi's project-trust prompt in advance: approve (--approve, loads the
# project's .pi/ settings, extensions, skills and .agents/skills) or ignore
# (--no-approve, leaves them out). Either way no dialog. Default: approve if
# HERD_AUTO_TRUST=1, otherwise ignore.
# HERD_PI_PROJECT_TRUST=ignore

# Pre-trust the working directory for backends with a trust dialog (0|1,
# default 0). A trusted folder makes the backend load the project's own
# configuration, skills and hooks — code and instructions from the repository.
# At 1: codex (-c projects=… for this session), muse (--trust-workspace for this
# session), grok (entry in ~/.grok/trusted_folders.toml, PERMANENT) and pi
# (--approve, unless HERD_PI_PROJECT_TRUST says otherwise). At 0 codex, grok
# and muse ask and the orchestrator answers the dialog; pi gets --no-approve
# (no dialog, project resources stay unloaded). Enable only for repositories
# whose configuration you trust.
# HERD_AUTO_TRUST=0

# Permission mode for claude/grok started with --role impl (default:
# acceptEdits). Research agents stay in plan mode. An explicit
# "start ... --permission-mode M" overrides this for both roles.
# HERD_IMPL_PERMISSION_MODE=acceptEdits

# --- Panes and housekeeping -------------------------------------------------

# Open a new tab once the current one has this many panes (default 4).
# HERD_MAX_PER_TAB=4

# How start launches a backend: agent (herdr agent start), run (pane run with
# a command file) or auto (default: run on Windows, agent elsewhere).
# HERD_START_VIA=auto

# start/exec/run delete log folders under ${XDG_RUNTIME_DIR:-${TMPDIR:-/tmp}}/herd-<uid>/
# older than this many days (default 7; 0 = never).
# HERD_LOG_KEEP_DAYS=7

# start/exec/run delete entries in .herd/ unchanged for this many days
# (default 14; 0 = never). Question files are kept.
# HERD_WORKDIR_KEEP_DAYS=14

# --- Watching ---------------------------------------------------------------

# Observation engine for watch/wait: auto (default) or events.
# HERD_WATCH_ENGINE=auto

# 1 = watch/wait also raise a herdr notification for every action line they
# print (default off). Read by the Python engine, so it must be exported.
# export HERD_NOTIFY=1
